Sure, you can use the following JavaScript code to reload the current page every 2 minutes (120,000 milliseconds). You can simply paste this code into your browser's console:

```javascript
setInterval(function() {
    location.reload();
}, 120000);
```

This code sets up an interval that will call the `location.reload()` function every 120,000 milliseconds (which is equivalent to 2 minutes), causing the page to reload automatically at that frequency.

If you want to stop this automatic reloading later, you can clear the interval using:

```javascript
clearInterval(intervalId);
```

Where `intervalId` is the ID returned by the `setInterval` function
